1
00:00:00,660 --> 00:00:01,620
Mark 8

2
00:00:01,620 --> 00:00:07,860
In those days, when again a great crowd had gathered, and they had nothing to eat,

3
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:10,660
he called his disciples to him and said to them,

4
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:16,700
I have compassion on the crowd, because they have been with me now three days and have nothing to eat.

5
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:21,140
And if I send them away hungry to their homes, they will faint on the way,

6
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:23,640
and some of them have come from far away.

7
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:26,180
And his disciples answered him,

8
00:00:26,180 --> 00:00:30,420
How can one feed these people with bread here in this desolate place?

9
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:32,340
And he asked them,

10
00:00:32,680 --> 00:00:34,680
How many loaves do you have?

11
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:36,060
They said,

12
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:37,200
Seven.

13
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:40,380
And he directed the crowd to sit down on the ground.

14
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:43,820
And he took the seven loaves, and having given thanks,

15
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:47,680
he broke them and gave them to his disciples to set before the people,

16
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:49,820
and they set them before the crowd.

17
00:00:50,420 --> 00:00:52,180
And they had a few small fish,

18
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:56,160
and having blessed them, he said that these also should be set before them.

19
00:00:56,860 --> 00:00:58,680
And they ate and were satisfied.

20
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:02,900
And they took up the broken pieces left over, seven baskets full.

21
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:07,100
And there were about four thousand people, and he sent them away.

22
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:12,460
And immediately he got into the boat with his disciples and went to the district of Dalmanutha.

23
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:17,180
The Pharisees came and began to argue with him,

24
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:19,940
seeking from him a sign from heaven to test him.

25
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:23,240
And he sighed deeply in his spirit and said,

26
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:26,160
Why does this generation seek us?

27
00:01:26,180 --> 00:01:27,460
Why does this generation seek us?

28
00:01:27,460 --> 00:01:31,180
Truly I say to you, no sign will be given to this generation.

29
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:35,820
And he left them, got into the boat again, and went to the other side.

30
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:41,600
Now they had forgotten to bring bread, and they had only one loaf with them in the boat.

31
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:43,880
And he cautioned them, saying,

32
00:01:44,740 --> 00:01:49,580
Watch out! Beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and the leaven of Herod.

33
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:54,300
And they began discussing with one another the fact that they had no bread,

34
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:56,120
and Jesus, aware of this,

35
00:01:56,180 --> 00:01:56,740
said to them,

36
00:01:57,300 --> 00:02:00,300
Why are you discussing the fact that you have no bread?

37
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:03,200
Do you not yet perceive or understand?

38
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:05,340
Are your hearts hardened?

39
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:10,020
Having eyes do you not see, and having ears do you not hear?

40
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:15,440
And do you not remember, when I broke the five loaves for the five thousand,

41
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:19,240
how many baskets full of broken pieces did you take up?

42
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:21,560
They said to him,

43
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:22,660
Twelve.

44
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:25,260
And the seven for the four thousand.

45
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:26,160
How many baskets full of broken pieces did you take up?

46
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:28,880
How many baskets full of broken pieces did you take up?

47
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:30,540
And they said to him,

48
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:31,840
Seven.

49
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:33,820
And he said to them,

50
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:36,640
Do you not yet understand?

51
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:40,260
And they came to Bethsaida,

52
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:44,700
and some people brought to him a blind man and begged him to touch him.

53
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:48,740
And he took the blind man by the hand and led him out of the village.

54
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:53,080
And when he had spit on his eyes and laid his hands on him, he asked him,

55
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:55,220
Do you see anything?

56
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:57,800
And he looked up and said,

57
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:05,100
I see men, but they look like trees walking.

58
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:10,440
Then Jesus laid his hands on his eyes again, and he opened his eyes,

59
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:13,580
his sight was restored, and he saw everything clearly.

60
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:16,160
And he sent him to his home, saying,

61
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:18,680
Do not even enter the village.

62
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:24,920
And Jesus went on with his disciples to the villages of Caesarea Philippi,

63
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:27,780
and on the way he asked his disciples,

64
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:30,720
Who do people say that I am?

65
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:32,500
And they told him,

66
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:35,060
John the Baptist, and others say Elijah,

67
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:37,280
and others one of the prophets.

68
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:39,140
And he asked them,

69
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:41,720
But who do you say that I am?

70
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:43,480
Peter answered him,

71
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:45,440
You are the Christ.

72
00:03:46,060 --> 00:03:49,440
And he strictly charged them to tell no one about him,

73
00:03:49,660 --> 00:03:53,760
and he began to teach them that the Son of Man must suffer many things

74
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:55,200
and be rejected by the Lord.

75
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:55,700
And he said to them,

76
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:57,740
I will be rejected by the elders and the chief priests and the scribes,

77
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:01,420
and be killed, and after three days rise again.

78
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:03,560
And he said this plainly.

79
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:06,540
And Peter took him aside and began to rebuke him.

80
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,860
But turning and seeing his disciples, he rebuked Peter and said,

81
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:13,720
Get behind me, Satan,

82
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:16,720
for you are not setting your mind on the things of God,

83
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:18,540
but on the things of man.

84
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:22,460
And calling the crowd to him with his disciples, he said to them,

85
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:25,100
If anyone would come after me,

86
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:28,960
let him deny himself and take up his cross and follow me.

87
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:32,580
For whoever would save his life will lose it.

88
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:37,420
But whoever loses his life for my sake and the gospels will save it.

89
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:42,880
For what does it profit a man to gain the whole world and forfeit his soul?

90
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:46,140
For what can a man give in return for his soul?

91
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:52,400
For whoever is ashamed of me and of my words in this adulterous and sinful generation,

92
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:55,180
of him will the Son of Man also be ashamed,

93
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:59,260
when he comes in the glory of his Father with the holy angels.

